==== hyperbricks yaml {!{hypermedia}} ====
hypermedia:
  - type: hypermedia
  - text_10:
      - type: text
      - value: HELLO WORLD!
  - bodytag: <body id="main">|</body>
  - route: index
==== explainer ====
Special body enclosure with use of a pipe symbol |. Please note that this will not work when a template is applied. In that case, you have to add the bodytag in the template.
==== expected json ====
{
  "BodyTag": "<body id=\"main\">|</body>",
  "Cache": "",
  "ConfigCategory": "",
  "ConfigType": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "ContentType": "",
  "Cookies": null,
  "Doctype": "",
  "Enclose": "",
  "Favicon": "",
  "Head": null,
  "Headers": null,
  "HtmlTag": "",
  "HyperBricksFile": "",
  "HyperBricksKey": "",
  "HyperBricksPath": "",
  "Index": 0,
  "Items": null,
  "MetaDocDescription": "",
  "NoCache": false,
  "Route": "index",
  "Section": "",
  "Static": "",
  "Template": null,
  "Title": ""
}

==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <body id="main">
    HELLO WORLD!
  </body>
</html>
